WEBVTT

00:26.210 --> 00:28.670
Well, when we owe each other 100 favors,

00:28.670 --> 00:31.010
we'll listen to each other no matter what, okay?

00:32.010 --> 00:33.280
Whatever I want?

00:43.140 --> 00:53.400
First, second, third, fourth, fifth, sixth, seventh, eighth,

00:53.690 --> 00:59.340
ninth, tenth, eleventh, twelfth, thirteenth...

01:08.010 --> 01:17.960
92, 93, 94, 95, 96, 97, 98, 99,

01:22.490 --> 01:23.750
100.

01:25.810 --> 01:28.130
Here you go, hurry up and tell me.

01:28.710 --> 01:30.560
Your wish.

01:31.010 --> 01:32.990
But, Ken-chan...

01:33.410 --> 01:35.590
It's the rule, it can't be helped.

01:35.810 --> 01:38.980
Come on, it's already been a hundred times,
hurry up and tell me.

01:39.710 --> 01:40.570
But...

01:47.510 --> 01:48.660
Thank you.

01:49.110 --> 01:53.930
What are you talking about, I didn't mean anything weird.

01:55.610 --> 01:58.450
Well, just like... that...

01:58.910 --> 01:59.860
That?

02:00.610 --> 02:02.860
Yeah, that... that.

02:03.510 --> 02:04.550
What's that?

02:04.590 --> 02:09.030
Well... anyway, let's go fix the field first.

02:15.910 --> 02:20.660
Folk Dance and Overlapping Hearts

02:28.210 --> 02:29.610
Good afternoon.

02:31.810 --> 02:33.550
Welcome, Hikari-san.

02:35.210 --> 02:36.700
Kenji hasn't come yet?

02:36.810 --> 02:37.680
What's up?

02:37.910 --> 02:43.720
Well, it's hot staying at home, and I wanted Kenji to take me out for a spin.

02:45.210 --> 02:47.650
Next up is the typhoon warning everybody has been concerned about.

02:48.310 --> 02:49.060
Fujiko-san.

02:49.610 --> 02:50.150
Yes?

02:50.410 --> 02:54.670
The typhoon that developed four days ago is now advancing with severe winds and storms.

02:54.810 --> 02:59.120
It's also getting stronger as it travels north.

02:59.610 --> 03:02.550
Please watch the news later for an update.

02:59.610 --> 03:04.980
--(Typhoon News)

03:03.110 --> 03:04.980
Next, we have satellite pictures of the weather.

03:05.410 --> 03:06.640
Here you go.

03:06.810 --> 03:08.080
Yeah, thank you.

03:08.710 --> 03:12.990
He left with Konoe-san just now.

03:13.210 --> 03:16.570
What? That's boring. He already had plans with her?

03:17.510 --> 03:20.920
What's their true relationship? Tell me.

03:21.610 --> 03:28.110
Well, what can I say, they still have an ambivalent attitude towards each other.

03:28.310 --> 03:29.820
Indeed.

03:30.510 --> 03:33.560
I guess they're the only ones who don't really feel anything.

03:36.510 --> 03:41.080
Hey, Ken-chan, look, look, they're so cute.

04:22.510 --> 04:23.920
Ah, not bad.

04:24.610 --> 04:28.770
No, no, I don't want those, just looking.

04:30.110 --> 04:34.320
Besides, I'm already wearing this one.

04:34.670 --> 04:37.920
This one is my favorite.

04:58.410 --> 05:00.080
Thank you, Ken-chan.

05:33.310 --> 05:36.010
Is Sakura-san still doing okay?

05:36.210 --> 05:37.030
Yeah.

05:40.610 --> 05:42.950
But... But...

05:43.510 --> 05:47.360
You can't always think, "That's fine."

06:24.310 --> 06:25.730
Hey, Ken-chan.

06:26.010 --> 06:26.820
What's up?

06:27.110 --> 06:29.580
Can you take me to the field?

06:30.110 --> 06:32.180
Sure, but what are you going to do in the field?

06:32.310 --> 06:33.910
Well, please.

06:44.130 --> 06:48.480
Hey, Nanami, what are we going to do with this much? You won't be able to eat them all.

06:53.210 --> 06:57.810
I think Sakura-san would be really happy if I sent these to her.

06:59.410 --> 07:00.310
Nanami...

07:03.110 --> 07:04.270
I can't?

07:05.310 --> 07:07.910
Sure, since we have to send these to her anyway.

07:08.900 --> 07:12.680
How about we send our proud, "Nanami special" to her as well?

07:13.710 --> 07:15.750
Yeah, I'll go take a look.

07:20.510 --> 07:22.850
This will be a whole lot easier.

07:30.010 --> 07:32.470
Why did you pick so much?

07:32.810 --> 07:35.310
I can finally show off a bit.

07:36.910 --> 07:39.300
Ken-chan, drive carefully.

07:41.510 --> 07:46.950
My favorite bike... My favorite bike turned into this!

08:12.610 --> 08:13.710
Hey, Nanami.

08:15.710 --> 08:17.270
What, Ken-chan?

08:17.850 --> 08:21.500
Do you want to go for a spin to somewhere far from here?

08:23.510 --> 08:27.990
We still have some time, and since Misora's in the store, that should be fine too.

08:28.710 --> 08:29.930
It's hard finding a chance to go out like this.

08:30.110 --> 08:32.550
How about we go to the camping place we went to last time?

08:38.810 --> 08:42.260
Hey, I don't think I got a chance to dance with you.

08:42.710 --> 08:43.680
That's why...

08:47.810 --> 08:49.980
If you don't want to go, that's all right.

08:53.510 --> 08:55.270
Hmm, okay.

08:58.210 --> 08:59.140
All right.

09:01.610 --> 09:06.120
Ken-chan, drive carefully!

09:26.290 --> 09:27.920
What's your zodiac sign, Hikari-chan?

09:28.310 --> 09:29.160
Pisces.

09:29.660 --> 09:32.890
Hmm, "Calamity strikes through the mouth."

09:33.210 --> 09:34.230
What's that?

09:34.410 --> 09:40.090
Hey, look. This week, the love index for Kenji and Konoe-san is pretty good.

09:40.310 --> 09:41.420
Really?

09:41.710 --> 09:45.300
It says the love index for both Virgo and Taurus is going up.

09:45.410 --> 09:48.070
And there will be a dramatic, loving scene.

09:48.310 --> 09:49.680
It's cool, huh?

09:50.010 --> 09:54.950
Huh? But it says both of those zodiac signs should watch out for their health.

09:55.230 --> 09:56.860
And watch out for storms.

09:57.710 --> 09:59.280
What does this mean?

09:59.510 --> 10:00.420
Who knows?

10:01.510 --> 10:04.360
Well, how about it, Hikari-sensei?

10:04.510 --> 10:06.850
What do you think after seeing that prediction?

10:07.210 --> 10:09.430
Well, it can't be one hundred percent right.

10:11.810 --> 10:17.420
Anyway, that useless Kenji won't do anything as romantic as a TV drama show.

10:34.260 --> 10:36.800
Don't look for us. (smile) Just kidding, we'll be back before dinner. Sorry, but can you please put these vegetables into the fridge. -- Nanami

10:40.050 --> 10:42.220
Maybe their relationship really is developing.

10:42.610 --> 10:43.350
N-No way.

10:43.710 --> 10:48.500
If they do, I'll eat peanuts through my nose, and I'll walk around town on my hands for a week.

10:53.610 --> 10:55.400
Huh? Now?

11:08.810 --> 11:10.140
Why are you so ceremonious?

11:10.170 --> 11:14.230
At least discuss it with me, your best friend, before you take action.

11:14.270 --> 11:15.710
Who's your best friend?

11:15.710 --> 11:18.110
You jerk, if something good happens, don't forget to tell me!

11:18.110 --> 11:19.980
Dude, you're mistaken!

11:29.710 --> 11:30.800
It feels good.

11:31.110 --> 11:32.920
Yeah, it's so beautiful.

11:33.110 --> 11:34.210
You're not scared?

11:37.710 --> 11:42.380
That's fine, we'll have to buy presents for the others.

11:43.010 --> 11:43.640
Yeah.

12:08.310 --> 12:09.650
Hey, what was that just now?

12:09.810 --> 12:12.560
Ah, that? That was a greeting.

12:12.710 --> 12:15.490
Greeting? A peace sign?

12:15.510 --> 12:17.620
Yeah, that's what you do when you pass by.

12:18.210 --> 12:19.950
You can try it next time, okay?

12:21.510 --> 12:23.860
I-It's a little embarrassing.

12:27.110 --> 12:29.990
Ah, that is, ah, w-wait up!

12:31.380 --> 12:32.650
Peace!

12:44.510 --> 12:48.300
Hey, Nanami, you misunderstood me.

12:48.610 --> 12:54.480
Peace! Peace! Peace!

12:55.510 --> 12:57.040
Ah, it was really embarrassing.

12:57.510 --> 13:02.530
Huh, why? It was all your fault since you didn't explain it to me clearly.

13:02.810 --> 13:06.590
Nanami, you're pretty bold sometimes.

13:06.910 --> 13:08.620
That's not true.

13:08.710 --> 13:13.090
Like today, you run off to somewhere like this without telling your mom.

13:13.210 --> 13:16.110
That's because you told me to come along.

13:16.710 --> 13:19.950
So, you're the type that does whatever other people say?

13:20.010 --> 13:22.520
That's not true...

13:25.210 --> 13:27.750
It's because you invited me.

13:32.910 --> 13:36.650
Because you invited me... that's why I came.

14:01.010 --> 14:01.610
Huh?

14:02.310 --> 14:03.470
What's wrong?

14:03.710 --> 14:04.790
This is weird.

14:09.910 --> 14:12.300
We should still have gas left.

14:12.410 --> 14:13.860
Is it broken?

14:56.670 --> 14:59.750
The sun is setting already, what should we do?

15:00.010 --> 15:03.640
We're here anyway, so let's get going.

15:04.610 --> 15:05.460
All right.

15:07.010 --> 15:08.040
Get on, Nanami.

15:23.210 --> 15:28.110
Ah? Walk upside down with your nose...? Use peanuts to walk around town for a week?

15:28.150 --> 15:30.140
What the heck are you talking about?

15:30.310 --> 15:32.610
I can't talk to you. Hand it over to Suzuka!

15:39.850 --> 15:46.060
Hey, is that Suzuka? The bike is broken. It seems that I can't come back tonight.

15:47.010 --> 15:49.570
Hello? Are you listening to me?

15:50.010 --> 15:52.740
Nanami is with me now, please make an excuse to Dad, okay?

15:52.740 --> 15:53.570
It's me!

15:57.010 --> 15:57.780
You jerk!

16:01.710 --> 16:07.150
Yeah, I know. I'll take care of the bike, don't worry.

16:08.110 --> 16:10.390
Yeah, yeah, I'll talk to you later.

16:11.710 --> 16:13.780
So you got in trouble?

16:14.910 --> 16:18.110
Well, it's all right, but I guess he'll scold me when I get back.

16:18.510 --> 16:19.590
Are you going to be okay?

16:19.710 --> 16:22.960
Don't worry. Anyway, what's up with the room?

16:24.160 --> 16:25.460
W-Well...

16:31.410 --> 16:33.450
A double room isn't a good choice...

16:33.710 --> 16:37.430
Well, hmm... this is the only room they have left.

16:40.510 --> 16:44.150
I see, well, we have no choice.

16:44.610 --> 16:46.350
A-Anyway, let's get into the room first.

16:49.510 --> 16:54.180
I'm going to Konoe-san's house, you can have your dinner first.

16:57.710 --> 16:58.720
Stay overnight?

17:10.130 --> 17:11.080
Kenji-san.

17:11.540 --> 17:14.690
Even though I've no talent... please take care of me.

17:26.010 --> 17:28.520
Nanami-san, I...

17:30.930 --> 17:32.480
Kenji-san...

17:42.480 --> 17:45.290
What's wrong? Your face looks so red.

17:46.280 --> 17:47.310
Nothing...

17:48.160 --> 17:51.250
Ah, you must've thought up some weird stuff.

17:51.780 --> 17:54.370
N-No, I didn't.

17:54.780 --> 17:57.620
You've reached that age too.

17:58.110 --> 17:59.390
Hikari-chan!

18:00.780 --> 18:02.450
I was joking, joking.

18:15.720 --> 18:17.160
Ah... well...

18:17.280 --> 18:18.940
W-What, Ken-chan?

18:19.580 --> 18:22.600
How about... we go to that place and take a look?

18:23.830 --> 18:25.330
Ah, yeah.

18:26.760 --> 18:31.410
Ah, the moon is so beautiful.

18:32.080 --> 18:33.680
Hmm, yeah.

18:35.680 --> 18:37.540
Ken-chan, thank you.

18:37.810 --> 18:38.380
Huh?

18:39.180 --> 18:41.710
Hmm, nothing.

18:42.160 --> 18:46.210
Ah, I really should've brought a radio with me.

20:09.490 --> 20:10.330
I love you...

20:20.780 --> 20:21.950
I was kidding.

20:41.080 --> 20:43.870
That hurts, Ken-chan.

20:46.080 --> 20:46.860
Nanami.

21:05.930 --> 21:07.460
K-Ken-chan.

21:08.030 --> 21:08.800
Huh? What is it?

21:08.930 --> 21:13.010
I want to go to the field, can you go with me?

21:13.130 --> 21:15.760
Of course, you don't have to ask me every time.

21:16.060 --> 21:17.720
Okay. Thank you.

21:17.760 --> 21:19.530
Hey, put on your hat before you go.

21:19.530 --> 21:20.670
Oh yeah!

21:20.830 --> 21:22.760
Nanami, you really are reckless.

21:22.920 --> 21:23.700
I am not.

21:23.930 --> 21:27.150
Next episode on Lamune:
Typhoon Night and the End of Summer

21:27.630 --> 21:30.300
Today, we'll have pumpkin and corn.

21:29.500 --> 21:34.490
 Thanks to the following:
Ripper: TCT66; Original Timer: nanaya; Original Typesetter: kiasushou; Original Chinese Subs for Extra Scenes: Fino; English Subs: C1Anime

21:30.530 --> 21:32.940
Ah, watermelon would be good too.

21:33.330 --> 21:34.490
I'll pass.
